+# Bridge downhill release - 2026-10-17
+
+The owner reports that descending from the bridge stays glued to the road and does not match the entry hop. The previous release explicitly required positive rising support, so it excluded the downhill crest. BD01 adds a shallow downhill tangent release, BD02 covers landing feedback, and BD03 preserves entry, replay/rewind and version isolation.
+
+The final change gives the car a brief lift as the descending deck falls away. It adds no upward kick. Fast controlled descents across all five cars measure 9.5-21.2 cm of clearance and 0.158-0.267 seconds in the air; the Compact's 24 m/s standard-span pass measures about 16.8 cm. Slow 3 m/s crossings remain planted. Original entry snapshots are exact in both directions for all five cars.
+
+Eight bounded candidate arcs use the shared actual axle support. A single 37-double scratch field (296 bytes) predicts every canonical tick through the short landing window, preventing an early invisible skip followed by a missed crest. The chosen constant downward acceleration fits the short game-scale ramp; it is not a claim of literal Earth-gravity simulation. Actual motion remains a world-space ballistic arc. The existing 24-tick cooldown still suppresses repeated releases at one crest, while an entry landing can no longer hide a separate downhill crest on a short span. Low-speed ground-level layer changes cannot trigger a hop.
+
+Landing stores contact speed relative to the descending deck as a presentation observer. Suspension and the existing chassis thump use that contact speed with a 2.5 m/s feedback bound, avoiding hard-impact sparks and a violent body slam from an otherwise shallow supported hop. Real wall/contact impulses keep their independent feedback. A later ordinary jump hazard clears this downhill feedback context and retains its original launch and flight.
+
+Physics arcade-planar-0.66 pins the change. The outer 24-entry snapshot and input/proof schemas remain; the nested jump tuple adds fitted gravity and downhill context. The existing property-based rewind captures them and the presentation observer. Bridge/road geometry, layers/rails/underpasses, Desert recess, tire marks, camera, car handling and existing boards remain. No new world or cache is introduced. The verifier already stages the shared helper; no staging-list change is needed.
+
+Actual pinned Godot 4.7.2 checks with isolated local APPDATA:
+
+- Focused downhill suite: 623 headless, 623 Compatibility, 623 Mobile checks pass. All 64 controlled cases reproduce zero downhill clearance in frozen physics0.65 and verify the new restrained arc, both directions, five axle sizes, short/long/rotated spans, slow contact, ignored airborne controls, every-tick JSON replay, downhill rewind/reset, unchanged entry snapshots, later jump-hazard feedback, actual native presentation, pause stability and landing sound/suspension behavior.
+- Original whole-bridge jump suite: 453 checks pass with per-flight gravity verified. Its new output-directory option preserves the original 2026-10-16 captures and measurements.
+- Existing bridge contacts16, checkpoint layers259, entry258, exit2527 and rewind61 pass. Actual Compact races complete five Dust cloud laps in29154 ticks and five Over and under laps in25677 ticks.
+- Whole-project parser and final isolated verifier results are recorded in report.json. Both archived physics0.50/rules20 replay and current-version rejection checks pass; their historical inputs/documents remain unchanged.
+- Broader headless vehicle audio: 1454 assertions, one failure at `pause suspends loop playback`. An isolated original/current comparison reproduces `stream_paused=false` in both versions, with two comparison checks passing. This independent clean-pass limitation remains; the assertion is not weakened.
+
+Matched native views: [before](evidence/bridge-descent-2026-10-17/before-gl_compatibility.png), [after](evidence/bridge-descent-2026-10-17/after-gl_compatibility.png), [Mobile after](evidence/bridge-descent-2026-10-17/after-mobile.png). They use scripted desktop practice frames with synthetic frame timing, not FPS or hitch evidence.
+
+Retained initial failures exposed a premature tiny Kart release, insufficient sparse arc-clearance sampling, and a low-speed ground-layer change at the bridge mouth. Full tick clearance plus the crest/low-speed guards correct these without weakening the visibility/planted assertions. One run overlapped an unrelated Night texture being introduced and found its preload file temporarily absent; subsequent native runs and parser succeed. The pause comparison's first dynamic source load retained CRLF around its class declaration; newline normalization corrects it. Initial logs remain.
+
+[report.json](evidence/bridge-descent-2026-10-17/report.json) lists changed files, actual commands/results, hashes and the task-only review patch. Owner driving feel, physical-phone acceptance and matching client/verifier rollout remain. This task performed no phone attachment check/test, APK, live backend mutation or deployment.
